{"page":446,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.37889,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"432 Chapter 7: Integrals and Transcendental Functions"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09343,"w":0.593,"h":0.02816,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Equation (3) is separable if ƒ can be expressed as a product of a function of x and a function of y. The differential equation then has the form"},{"x":0.56634,"y":0.13749,"w":0.10224,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = g(x)H(y)."},{"x":0.70619,"y":0.13883,"w":0.10395,"h":0.02175,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"g is a function of x; H is a function of y."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.17786,"w":0.27719,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"When we rewrite this equation in the form"},{"x":0.57901,"y":0.20655,"w":0.06618,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = g(x)"},{"x":0.61892,"y":0.21199,"w":0.15187,"h":0.02431,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"h(y), H(y) = 1 h(y)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.2469,"w":0.53943,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"its differential form allows us to collect all y terms with dy and all x terms with dx:"},{"x":0.55781,"y":0.26926,"w":0.11996,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"h(y) dy = g(x) dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.29296,"w":0.34469,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Now we simply integrate both sides of this equation:"},{"x":0.5551,"y":0.32297,"w":0.06277,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"h(y) dy ="},{"x":0.64514,"y":0.32364,"w":0.26711,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"g(x) dx. (4)"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.35433,"w":0.59294,"h":0.02815,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"After completing the integrations, we obtain the solution y defined implicitly as a function of x."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.38504,"w":0.5931,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The justification that we can simply integrate both sides in Equation (4) is based on the Substitution Rule (Section 5.5):"},{"x":0.63026,"y":0.42397,"w":0.06199,"h":0.02246,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"h(y(x))dy"},{"x":0.5425,"y":0.43295,"w":0.06277,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"h(y) dy ="},{"x":0.67683,"y":0.43362,"w":0.03299,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dxdx"},{"x":0.63221,"y":0.46233,"w":0.0819,"h":0.02246,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"h(y(x)) g(x)"},{"x":0.77444,"y":0.46563,"w":0.02614,"h":0.02479,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx ="},{"x":0.80656,"y":0.46563,"w":0.022,"h":0.02489,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"g(x) h(y)"},{"x":0.67878,"y":0.47199,"w":0.06199,"h":0.02009,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"h(y(x))dx"},{"x":0.63464,"y":0.51803,"w":0.04985,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"g(x) dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.56622,"w":0.32289,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 1 Solve the differential equation"},{"x":0.54137,"y":0.59278,"w":0.18238,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"dy dx = (1 + y)ex, y 7 -1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.65915,"w":0.58893,"h":0.02899,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Solution Since 1 + y is never zero for y 7 -1, we can solve the equation by separat- ing the variables."},{"x":0.58346,"y":0.69637,"w":0.10254,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"dy dx = (1 + y)ex"},{"x":0.55911,"y":0.72201,"w":0.32763,"h":0.0603,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"Treat dy/dx as a quotient of differentials and multiply both sides by dx. dy 1 + y = ex dx Divide by (1 + y)."},{"x":0.58354,"y":0.72841,"w":0.12196,"h":0.01728,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dy = (1 + y)ex dx"},{"x":0.55911,"y":0.78973,"w":0.08015,"h":0.03329,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"dy 1 + y = L"},{"x":0.64304,"y":0.79491,"w":0.20158,"h":0.01727,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"ex dx Integrate both sides."},{"x":0.53354,"y":0.82176,"w":0.34779,"h":0.02303,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"ln(1 + y) = ex + C C represents the combined constants of integration."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.8595,"w":0.34603,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The last equation gives y as an implicit function of x."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.90356,"w":0.32951,"h":0.02246,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 2 Solve the equation y(x + 1) dy"},{"x":0.63741,"y":0.90807,"w":0.10766,"h":0.02522,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx = x(y2 + 1)."}]}